examples.solution_text:
For (a), use identical triangular ends. Their top corners join to form the ridge shown by the middle line in the top view.
For (b), use identical trapezium ends with narrower tops. The two inside lines in the top view mark the edges of the flat top face.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=9mm,y=9mm,draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
% Models: listed front polygons at z=0, identical rear polygons at their respective depths.
% Faces: both end polygons plus corresponding lateral quadrilaterals.
% Projection (x,y,z) -> (x+0.3z,y+0.2z); viewer (0.3,0.2,-1).
% (a) depth 3.5.
\draw (0,0)--(2.8,0)--(1.4,2.2)--cycle;
\draw (2.8,0)--(3.85,0.7)--(2.45,2.9)--(1.4,2.2);
\draw[dashed] (0,0)--(1.05,0.7)--(3.85,0.7) (1.05,0.7)--(2.45,2.9);
\path (1.9,-0.3) node[below] {(a)};
\begin{scope}[shift={(5.5,0)}]
% (b) depth 3.8.
\draw (0,0)--(3.4,0)--(2.7,2)--(0.7,2)--cycle;
\draw (3.4,0)--(4.54,0.76)--(3.84,2.76)--(2.7,2);
\draw (0.7,2)--(1.84,2.76)--(3.84,2.76);
\draw[dashed] (0,0)--(1.14,0.76)--(4.54,0.76) (1.14,0.76)--(1.84,2.76);
\path (2.2,-0.3) node[below] {(b)};
